                <pb facs="0717" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1946v04/pg705"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">C.P.(Gen)Doc.1.J.17.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article 74 bis</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-outside-research" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1946-10-15T23:59:59+01:00" notBefore="1946-07-29T00:00:00+01:00"
                        >undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>Insert the following in the financial clauses of the Peace Treaty with Italy:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p><hi rendition="#italic">Article</hi> … “Italy shall undertake to pay in
                            gold to the Bank of Greece within three months of the coming into force
                            of the present Treaty the sum of 64,800,000 dollars (1938 value), to
                            which the advances <pb facs="0718" n="706" xml:id="pg706"/> made by the
                            Bank of Greece to the Italian occupation authorities amount, in addition
                            to the occupation expenses borne by Greece under the agreement of March
                            14, 1942, between the German and Italian Governments, and all subsequent
                            modifications thereto.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
            </div>
        </body>
